whole, you'd have a portfolio with the beta of the mutual fund.  If
you tend to bet optimistically, as folks here probably would, on
claims suggesting that the market will do better than folks expect,
then your beta will be higher, as should your average (but *not*
average log) return.  

Actually, to gain a higher average return, you should bet on
conjunctions of various claims you believe more than others.  More
details on this and other related stuff in my long standard paper,
"Could Gambling Save Science", available from me.

Robin Hanson

